  "title": "Mamluk seizure of power in Egypt",
  "summary": "In May 1250, after the Ayyubid heir Turan Shah tried to replace his father's mamluk officers with his own men, those officers assassinated him. They first backed his father's widow Shajar al-Durr, and the officer Aybak was then acclaimed sultan. Mamluk rule over Egypt followed and lasted until 1517.",
